Use the **data-analyst** subagent to run the **`usability-analytics`** canon on $ARGUMENTS: pull the
prototype instrumentation (PostHog events/funnels/cohorts + time-on-task, Microsoft Clarity
heatmaps/replays, post-task SEQ, the /results dashboard), benchmark task success / efficiency / SEQ /
drop-off against documented UX norms, triangulate quant with qual, and report with statistical caution.

Always exclude practice/QA runs (`is_test`). Return the skill's output: snapshot (data · range · n) ·
metric scorecard vs benchmark · behavioral findings (quant + paired Clarity evidence) · validation
verdicts (validated / invalidated / inconclusive + confidence) · recommendations routed to
`ux-designer` · data-quality caveats. A behavioral problem that traces to a component defect is a DS
gap — route it.

Defer to the agent + skill — do not restate the benchmarks here.
